message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
title: "HC/SGN: Hypermetric Number System and Integer Quantization Kernels (Archived)"
abstract: >-
  A custom number-type system built on hypermetric (ultrametric) space:
  multi-level byte arrays form a 256-/65536-way tree where lexicographic
  order is the ultrametric distance and prefixes are ultrametric balls.
  Two tracks: (v0.1) the full SGN mainline — HC8/16/32/64 types, DC,
  HPDC engine/sandbox/trie/storage, pybind11 bindings, minimal-linkage
  MCU usage (time variables, exact records, flash-tolerant logging);
  (v0.2) the final C version of the neural-network quantization extension —
  HC8/HC16 integer matrix-multiply paths (int4/8/16, AVX2/FMA/AVX-VNNI),
  SBE block quantization, Conv2d fusion, multi-view storage.
  Status: archived. The hypermetric route for neural-network training was
  falsified by dual-library verification (ultrametric inequality violation
  rate ~100% for gradients); the repository is retained for its number
  types and forward quantization-inference results.
